WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.145
A screen reader should hear what changes, once. Not a clock, every second.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.044
As a step starts, the rider hears it once, in the card's own words: work, round one

00:00:15.044 --> 00:00:17.960
of eight, thirty seconds at level twenty-four.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.047
When Results opens, it says the result: you finished in twenty-six thirty-eight, and

00:00:28.047 --> 00:00:29.150
the XP earned.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:40.918
A dialog takes the focus and keeps it. The app behind it goes inert, and closing

00:00:40.918 --> 00:00:43.550
gives the focus back to what opened it.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:54.348
With reduced motion, nothing moves but a fade. The interval bar kept sliding; now it

00:00:54.348 --> 00:00:55.849
jumps to its place.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:06.745
Every screen is checked for motion on every run, beside the steps, the result and

00:01:06.745 --> 00:01:07.697
the dialog.

00:01:14.847 --> 00:01:17.170
Results, from a phone to the full screen.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:29.774
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:34.631
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:34.631 --> 00:01:36.302
every hill and interval.

00:01:36.647 --> 00:01:41.825
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:41.825 --> 00:01:47.273
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:50.263
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:50.608 --> 00:01:53.101
A custom workout lives under Profile.
